.TH GOFILE-PUBLISH 1 "2026-11-19" "gofile-publish" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gofile-publish \- upload .ts recordings to gofile.io, one folder per model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gofile-publish
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gofile-publish
scans a directory for
.B .ts
recordings, derives a model name from each filename prefix, and uploads every
file into a public gofile.io folder named after that model, under the account's
root folder.
.P
A free gofile account cannot list its own remote contents through the API, so
the script keeps a JSON state file that is the only record of what exists where:
model name to folder UUID and share code, plus one entry per uploaded file. A
re\-run skips files already recorded at the same byte size, so an interrupted
run resumes where it stopped.
.P
Uploads are delegated to
.BR curl (1)
so multi\-gigabyte files are streamed from disk instead of being buffered in
memory. gofile uploads are not resumable: an interrupted file restarts from
zero. Transfers are sequential, because the uplink saturates on a single stream
and extra concurrency only slows each one down.
.P
The model name is the filename prefix before the recording timestamp:
.IR abbytheran_2026-11-17_20-33-50_423.ts
becomes
.IR abbytheran .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Source directory. Default:
.IR /mnt/pve/Data_Storage/vr .
.TP
.BI \-\-root " UUID"
UUID of the account root folder. Required once; afterwards it is read from the
state file. The value is shown on the gofile account profile page.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Only process this model. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Stop after N successful uploads.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-size " GB"
Skip files smaller than this many decimal gigabytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
State file. Default:
.IR ~/.local/state/gofile-publish/state.json .
Delete it and the script loses track of existing folders and uploads.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-file " FILE"
File containing the gofile API token. Default:
.IR ~/.config/gofile/token .
The environment variable
.B GOFILE_TOKEN
takes precedence.
.TP
.BI \-\-manifest " FILE"
TSV of model, file count, total size and share link. Rewritten at the end of
every run. Default:
.IR ~/.local/state/gofile-publish/links.tsv .
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Print the per\-model plan and folder links without uploading anything. Does not
require a root folder.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Print only share links, one per line, for scripting.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS What it does
.IP \(bu 2
Creates one public folder per model under the account root, remembered in the
state file.
.IP \(bu 2
Uploads matching files into that folder, recording id, md5 and size.
.IP \(bu 2
Retries rate\-limited and transport failures up to three times.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.BR curl (1)
.IP \(bu 2
A gofile API token.
.SH EXAMPLES
See what would be uploaded, grouped by model:
.IP
.EX
gofile-publish \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
First real run for one model, after setting the root folder once:
.IP
.EX
gofile-publish \-\-root ecb747d3\-1610\-48a9\-815e\-9a42a77ad520 \-\-model abbytheran
.EE
.P
Upload everything that is not recorded yet:
.IP
.EX
gofile-publish
.EE
.P
Just the share links:
.IP
.EX
gofile-publish \-\-quiet
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All pending uploads succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
One or more uploads failed, or a required argument was missing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/gofile-publish/state.json
Folder and upload records. Losing it means losing the mapping of local files to
remote folders.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/gofile-publish/links.tsv
Last generated manifest.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gofile/token
API token, mode 600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gofile-publish-remote (1),
.BR curl (1)
.SH BUGS
gofile uploads cannot be resumed, so a dropped connection wastes the bytes sent
so far. Free accounts keep a file only while it is downloaded at least every ten
days, so old posts can lose their links.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
